<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Remarks">Remarks</span></h2>
<p>Using the following values for the "Trigger/Volume" options makes it easy to differentiate the volume types as each volume's colour in the area editor matches the colour of its icon in the object list and toolbar:
</p>
<dl><dd> <img alt="Audio volume icon.png" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/0/08/Audio_volume_icon.png" width="16" height="16" /> Audio Volume Fill Color = 0.25,0.25,0.75 </dd>
<dd> <img alt="Music volume icon.png" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/d/da/Music_volume_icon.png" width="16" height="16" /> Music Volume Fill Color = 0.75,0.75,0.25 </dd>
<dd> <img alt="Reverb volume icon.png" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/5/59/Reverb_volume_icon.png" width="16" height="16" /> Reverb Volume Fill Color = 0.75,0.25,0.25 </dd>
<dd> <img alt="Trigger volume icon.png" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/Wiki/assets/mw/images/b/b0/Trigger_volume_icon.png" width="16" height="16" /> Trigger Fill Color = 0.25,0.75,0.25</dd></dl>
